    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "When we multiply a vector, x, by a matrix, A, to create a new vector, y = Ax, A rotates and scales the original vector, x, into the new vector, y. A therefore describes a transformation of the original coordinate system of x into a new coordinate system, y (which has a different dimension from x unless A is square).",
